# Line endings are LF in the repo AND in the working tree, on every platform.
#
# Not a style preference. Three things in this repo parse their own source files with regexes that
# anchor on `$`, which does not match before a CRLF's `\r`:
#   · scripts/lib/catalog.mjs reads components/index.ts to build the catalog,
#   · prettier's endOfLine default is "lf", so a CRLF checkout fails `format:check` on every file,
#   · the CI job diffs generated files and would see a checkout artefact as a stale build.
# On Windows with the default `core.autocrlf=true`, all three broke at once. `eol=lf` overrides
# autocrlf, so a Windows clone now gets the same bytes CI does.
#
# The scripts were also made CRLF-tolerant. This file and that fix are deliberately redundant:
# neither should have to trust the other.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries git must never touch.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
